crates/segment (lightcraft-segment) ports the SAM 3 model code of Hugging Face Transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, src/transformers/models/sam3 and sam3_tracker),
Copyright The HuggingFace Team and Meta Platforms, Inc., licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The port was modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from Python/PyTorch to
Rust on candle and restructured; each ported file says so. Because of this, crates/segment is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE), not under the MIT option.

crates/search (lightcraft-search) ports the SigLIP model code of Hugging Face Transformers
(src/transformers/models/siglip), Copyright The HuggingFace Team and Google, licensed under the Apache
License 2.0, translated to Rust on candle by the LightCraft contributors (2026). It is licensed under the
Apache License 2.0 only. The SigLIP 2 weights (google/siglip2-base-patch16-224, Apache License 2.0 per its
model card) are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it: a user downloads them only when
they choose to. See docs/semantic-search.md.

The SAM 3 weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it. A user downloads
the facebook/sam3 checkpoint only when they choose to (in the app, or by hand), under Meta's SAM
License (https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3/blob/main/LICENSE), a separate, non-OSI
licence. See docs/ai-masks.md.

AI denoise weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it.
The default build offers user-supplied models only. The optional rawnind-model
feature offers a separately downloaded RawNIND UtNet2 Bayer checkpoint under
GPL-3.0 (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html), after the user accepts its terms.
Commercial use is subject to those terms, including applicable source, licence and
notice obligations on redistribution. Enabling that offer in releases remains a
maintainer decision. The ONNX reader and CPU/GPU executor are our Rust implementation;
no darktable, RawSpeed, LibRaw or other GPL decoder/runtime code is included.
crates/faces (lightcraft-faces) runs Google's MediaPipe Face Landmarker (BlazeFace detector and Face
Mesh V2) and follows MediaPipe's published face landmarker graph (https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe,
Apache License 2.0). Its TensorFlow Lite interpreter, kernels and zip reader are adapted from EffectCraft's
effectcraft-segment (same authors, MIT OR Apache-2.0), and read the .tflite FlatBuffer as laid out by the
TensorFlow Lite schema (Apache License 2.0). The face model file (face_landmarker.task, Apache License 2.0,
Google LLC) is not part of LightCraft and is never distributed with it: a user downloads it only when they
choose to (in the app, or by hand), checked against its published SHA-256. See docs/faces.md.
crates/restore (lightcraft-restore) ports two inference networks, translated from Python/PyTorch to
Rust on candle and modified by the LightCraft contributors (2026); each ported file says so:
SCUNet (https://github.com/cszn/SCUNet, models/network_scunet.py, Copyright Kai Zhang et al.,
Apache License 2.0; its Swin blocks derive from SwinIR, Apache-2.0) and SPAN
(https://github.com/hongyuanyu/SPAN, basicsr/archs/span_arch.py, Apache License 2.0, built on
BasicSR, Copyright 2018-2020 BasicSR Authors). crates/restore/src/pt.rs (a PyTorch checkpoint
reader) comes from the sibling EffectCraft project (MIT OR Apache-2.0). Because of the ports,
crates/restore is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE).

The AI denoise and super-resolution weights are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed
with it. A user downloads them only when they choose to: scunet_color_real_psnr.pth from the
SCUNet authors' KAIR release (no separate licence stated; see docs/ai-restore.md) and
2xNomosUni_span_multijpg.safetensors by Philip Hofmann, licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/; https://huggingface.co/Phips/2xNomosUni_span_multijpg).

crates/depth (lightcraft-depth) ports the Depth Anything V2 network code of Hugging Face Transformers
(https://github.com/huggingface/transformers, src/transformers/models/depth_anything and dinov2),
Copyright The HuggingFace Team, licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The port was modified by the
LightCraft contributors (2026): translated from Python/PyTorch to Rust on candle and restructured; the
file says so. Because of this, crates/depth is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only (LICENSE-APACHE),
not under the MIT option.

The Depth Anything V2 Small weights (depth-anything/Depth-Anything-V2-Small-hf, Apache License 2.0,
Copyright the Depth Anything authors, https://github.com/DepthAnything/Depth-Anything-V2) are not part of
LightCraft and are never distributed with it. A user downloads them only when they choose to (SHA-256
checked). The larger V2 models (Base, Large, Giant) are CC-BY-NC-4.0 and are never used. See
docs/depth-inpaint.md.

crates/inpaint (lightcraft-inpaint) runs MI-GAN (Picsart AI Research, MIT License, code and weights:
https://github.com/Picsart-AI-Research/MI-GAN) from its ONNX export with a small interpreter of its own, on
candle. The model file is not part of LightCraft and is never distributed with it; a user downloads it
only when they choose to (SHA-256 checked). MI-GAN was trained on Places2 and FFHQ; see docs/depth-inpaint.md
for what that means for the weights.

Builds made with craft-fonts (the optional CRAFT_FONTS_DIR build input; all official releases)
also embed the fonts listed in https://github.com/storytold/craft-fonts/blob/main/ATTRIBUTION.md
(the Japanese fonts BIZ UDPGothic, BIZ UDMincho and Shippori Mincho; the web build embeds only BIZ
UDPGothic Regular), under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Release packages include each font's
licence as OFL-<family>.txt.

crates/lens (lightcraft-lens) reads the lens calibrations of the lensfun project's lens database
(https://lensfun.github.io/, repository lensfun/lensfun, data/db/*.xml, revision
43f9e001ab66c4fcdd4f400463f13b72f94b2288), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0
licence (CC BY-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/). Only the database's data files are
used (converted to crates/lens/data/lens-profiles.json.z by crates/lens/examples/build_db.rs: XML to
compact JSON, focal range and widest aperture filled from the lens names where the entry lacked them);
none of the lensfun library's code (LGPL) is read, linked or copied. The converted data file remains a
separate file under CC BY-SA 3.0 (ShareAlike applies to adaptations of it); see crates/lens/data/README.md.

crates/people (lightcraft-people) runs InsightFace's ArcFace face-recognition networks (w600k_r50 of the buffalo_l
pack, w600k_mbf of the buffalo_s pack; https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface) from their ONNX files with the
interpreter of crates/inpaint. The weights are released by InsightFace for non-commercial research purposes only;
they are not part of LightCraft and are never distributed with it: a user downloads them only when they choose to
(SHA-256 checked), after being shown these terms. No InsightFace code is copied; the alignment template is a list
of ten coordinates.


crates/places (lightcraft-places) resolves GPS positions to country / region / city offline with data from
GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Files used: cities1000.zip, countryInfo.txt and
admin1CodesASCII.txt from https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/ (retrieved 2026-10-09), converted to
crates/places/data/places-cities.bin by crates/places/examples/build_db.rs (tab-separated text to a compact
binary table; kept per place: name, position, country, first-level division, population; all other columns
dropped). Required attribution: "Place data from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), CC BY 4.0, converted by
LightCraft." The data file stays a separate file loaded at run time; see crates/places/data/README.md.
